#: ../../source/incoming/routing.rst:519
msgid "Reverse Routing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/routing.rst:521
msgid ""
"Reverse routing allows you to define the controller and method, as well "
"as any parameters, that a link should go to, and have the router lookup "
"the current route to it. This allows route definitions to change without "
"you having to update your application code. This is typically used within"
" views to create links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/routing.rst:525
msgid ""
"For example, if you have a route to a photo gallery that you want to link"
" to, you can use the :php:func:`url_to()` helper function to get the "
"route that should be used. The first parameter is the fully qualified "
